Z||000007||Formula88||11-12-2001||02:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B>Hmm...I thought maybe you did an epoxy coating or something.  So, it's just a chip with a hold drilled in it and a ring put on it?  Sorry, not to sound cheap or anything, but I can do that on my own.  Good luck!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Don't even have to drill a hole.  They're already there from the factory.  Just take RAM stick, and attach your $0.79 hardware store key ring.  Done.  If people want to make their own, I'd recommend 30pin SIMMS.  I've made a few, and 72pin SIMMS are a little large for most men, and DIMMS are way too large.  This usually isn't a problem for the ladies if they carry their keys in a purse.  Most ladies I know have a huge collection of stuff on their keychain anyway.<P>I remember when you could find 1Mb and 4Mb 30pin SIMMS for $1 each online.  May be hard to find now, but could be a fun project.  They also make cool earrings.  Also, old CPU's, make good keychains, but you have to shave the pins off and drill a hole in the chip.  Kinda tricky, but looks neat when done.  <BR>||||reg||1
